# rota: seats in the pool that are NOT yours to spend.
#
# Copy to $CLAUDE_FAILOVER_HOME/reserved (default ~/.config/claude-failover/reserved).
# Machine-local, like `accounts` - it names your people and your servers, so it
# never belongs in the repo.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS. A pool can hold seats that still show plenty of quota and are
# still somebody else's: one pushed to a server that runs against it around the
# clock, one handed to a colleague. `rota accounts` ranks on quota, so without
# this it will confidently tell you to switch onto one of them. It did exactly
# that on 2026-08-25, recommending a seat handed over the day before.
#
# FORMAT: one seat per line.
#
#   <alias>  [owner]  [why...]
#
# `alias` matches the seat's alias in the accounts file. `owner` is a short tag
# shown in the table's NOTES column. Everything after it is free text for you.
# Blank lines and anything after a # are ignored.
#
# A seat is ALSO reserved if it carries a RESERVED file in its own config dir
# (see `rota reserve`, and the shim which reads the same file when it refuses to
# open a session there). The two sources are UNIONED, never "markers else this
# file" - otherwise the first box to grow a marker would silently un-reserve
# every seat named only here.
#
# Examples:
# runner-seat   ci-runner   pushed to the build host; a local pane starves it
# team-seat     alex        handed over 2026-01-14
